  "authorizationBoundary": "Existing human-approved generic plans add ordinary Service full-set dependency replacement and Registry activate/deactivate with empty typed parameters. Ordinary links retain complete native map-set CAS through the original shared SETLINKS mutation owner and commit tail, exact source/Stack/target identity and current Key/role ceilings, including strict nonnegative revision zero. Registry lifecycle retains exact native StoragePool registry identity, private configuration CAS, current owner/Key authority, persisted native process binding and fresh terminal reads; no credential writes or private configuration projection are admitted. The two added aiResourceChangePlan enum selectors do not add an HTTP tuple or native resource method/action/role grant. The existing INVALID_INPUT audit contract remains closed for exact native PortConflict. Published382 Agent/null-process fixes remain unchanged. This extraction is source-only; formal CI, compiled packaged schemas, immutable publication and native acceptance remain pending. Native typed-decision audit admits only the registered registry business target; storagePool and storageDriver remain rejected. A private native SETLINKS transaction owner now joins failure and completion into one release claim, guarantees finally-based unlock/provider release despite resource-cleanup exceptions, preserves the original registration failure, and recovers only exact confirmed-success same-thread markers before transaction or nontransaction writer actions; uncertain release state remains fail-closed and new retention until commit stays conditional. The existing SETLINKS native mutation owner acquires sorted bulk handler scopes iteratively without consumer-count recursion, retains transaction acquisitions until completion even after partial contention, and releases only each scope's acquired mutex. The native Lock interface adds a backward-compatible checked release default; StandardLock reports and quarantines observed checked physical-release failures while ordinary legacy release remains best effort. Exact unknown leases/diagnostics stay quarantined in this SETLINKS owner without provider-map policy changes or unsafe automatic retry; successful resource-cleanup faults remain recoverable. These local controls do not claim normal CI, packaged class qualification, publication, or native acceptance.",
